<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wei Zhongxian</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1568">1568</a>–<a href="/years/1627">1627</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Wei Si, Li Jinzhong</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wei Zhongxian was a Chinese court <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eunuch">eunuch</a> of the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming dynasty</a>, considered by most historians the most notorious eunuch in Chinese history, whose power under the Tianqi Emperor (r. 1620–1627) came to appear to rival the emperor's. Illiterate and perhaps of peasant or merchant birth, he entered palace service and grew close to the young Zhu Youjiao and his wet nurse, Madame Ke. As head of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-depot">Eastern Depot</a> and bearer of the emperor's edicts, he promoted and demoted hundreds of officials, while in 1625–1626 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/embroidered-uniform-guard">Embroidered Uniform Guard</a> tortured and killed leaders of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/donglin-movement">Donglin movement</a>. Exiled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chongzhen-emperor">Chongzhen Emperor</a> in 1627, he hanged himself when he learned he was to be arrested.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>A few rose to rule the court, as Wang Zhen, Liu Jin and <b>Wei Zhongxian</b> did.</blockquote><a href="/societies/ming-china">Social Hierarchy of Ming China</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Suning County, in what is now <a href="/countries/china">China</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/china">China</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=38.43,115.83&amp;year=1606" aria-label="Suning County on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7429 784 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Wei Zhongxian"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7879 1054h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7879 1054h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=38.43,115.83&amp;year=1606">What was here in 1606? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
